   "design": "Senders send electronic orders and label specimens with barcodes. Scanning a specimen matches it to its order and shows any mismatch, instead of the cytotechnologist comparing labels and forms by eye and typing the form. The laboratory system prints barcode labels for slides and vials. Clinical checks, calls about mismatches, the nonconformity log and holding specimens stay with the cytotechnologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Labels and forms were compared by eye and forms typed in.",
   "enabler_now": "Electronic orders, barcode matching and label printing.",
   "still_hard": "Senders with handwritten labels.",
   "human_edge": "Spotting a specimen that does not belong to this patient.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less comparing and typing; resolving mismatches stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "senders",
     "task": "Send specimens",
     "learn": "Whether mismatches fall."
    }
   ],
   "build_days": {
    "coding": "0-1",
    "integration": "1-2",
